==Rules==
{{ColosseumRule|Uniform Motion|12}}

==Battleground==
*3 [[Miz Devil]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Wild Doge]]s spawn after 21.33 seconds<sup>640f</sup>, delay 46.67~50 seconds<sup>1,400f~1,500f</sup>.
*2 [[Maawth]]s spawn after 28 seconds<sup>840f</sup>, delay 180~183.33 seconds<sup>5,400f~5,500f</sup>.
*1 [[THE FOLIVOREAN]] spawns as the boss after 46.67 seconds<sup>1,400f</sup>.
*1 [[Elephantidae Papaou]] spawns after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>.
*2 [[Kang Roo]]s spawn after 83.33 seconds<sup>2,500f</sup>, delay 100~103.33 seconds<sup>3,000f~3,100f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Miz Devil]]s spawn after 86.67 seconds<sup>2,600f</sup>, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
*1 [[Rain D.]] spawns after 113.33 seconds<sup>3,400f</sup>.

==Strategy==
With everything spawning on a timer and moving at the same 12 speed, the normally sluggish Elephantidae Papaou becomes a much greater threat, as little time is given to gather resources and most enemies here don't drop enough funding to support a constant stream of units that could otherwise cut through his HP. His Immunity to Knockback, Slow and Freeze further complicates things, as his constant attacks can and will allow the other threats (especially Rain D. and Wild Doge) to easily advance. With rushers being mostly ineffective, players should resort to DPS units that can safely outrange both Papaou and THE FOLIVOREAN while disposable specialists quickly remove the nasty peons.

Due to the tight startoff, a Rich Cat is recommended here. Sniper the Cat can also prove helpful, as it can still cause Papaou to flinch.

===Recommended Ubers===
*[[Tecoluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Lufalan]] - Lufalan stands at a very safe range of 720, far beyond the reach of any enemy here (even THE FOLIVOREAN's attacks reach only up to 500 range), and, despite having Single Attack, can possibly score many hits on the larger threats here, as the peons don't spawn very frequently. Its inconsistent Critical Hits (20%, up to 30% with talents) can tremendously speed up the fight when it occurs.

